From 39a036b142f4b530ab8776c14071b678dcb1f32f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 08:30:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] Grid-difference plan: the two measures added after the
 first look at a development site

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016zPE7K49ycKieo7wJdrBFN
---
 .../adaptive-simulation-quality/01-grid-difference/README.md  | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/studies/adaptive-simulation-quality/01-grid-difference/README.md b/studies/adaptive-simulation-quality/01-grid-difference/README.md
index d4b263b..5973299 100644
--- a/studies/adaptive-simulation-quality/01-grid-difference/README.md
+++ b/studies/adaptive-simulation-quality/01-grid-difference/README.md
@@ -35,6 +35,10 @@ fire's path, so D says where a gap has grown and E where it was made.
 (the 20 % of the whole domain with the highest score, as the quality map defines it), with the share the cells of the set would carry by size alone, and the most any set of that size could carry; (3) against **random sets of the same size**, against random sets
 with the same number of cells in each tenth of the arrival-time range, and against **the same set moved elsewhere** on the map (the eight symmetries of the square and wrap-around shifts, which keep the set's shape: complex cells and large differences both come in
 patches, so scattered random sets are too easy a comparison); (4) recall of the cells with the largest D (top 20 % of the scored cells) by the top-20 % set. Draws: 2000 random, 1000 time-matched, 1000 moved, 400 for the correlation; seeded.
+**Added after the first look at Katoomba (a development site; no hold-out site had been scored; committed before the other sites were scored):** random sets of the same size drawn from the whole domain
+carry 20 % of the difference by definition, but a set that holds cliff faces and ground the fire never reaches has fewer than 20 % of the scored cells, so that comparison also charges the set for cells the front never visits. Two things were added and both are
+reported next to it: the **lift per scored cell** (the share carried over the share of the scored cells the set holds; 1 is chance), tested against random sets with as many scored cells and against the moved set's own lift (the moved-set test of the share mixes the
+lift with how much of the burnt ground the moved set covers). The tests that treat cells as exchangeable (random sets) overstate the evidence, because both the difference and the complexity come in patches; the moved-set test is the one to read.
 
 **The tuned version.** Weights of the five groups on a grid of step 0.1 (1001 vectors), chosen to maximise the mean rank correlation with D over the development sites (30 m against 10 m, 8 h, both embers settings); its numbers on the hold-out sites are reported next to the score as defined.
 The best single group is chosen the same way.

